ZXV ROOT TRUST ANCHOR  —  TEMPLATE, NOT A REAL ANCHOR
=====================================================

This file is a placeholder. There is deliberately NO real trust anchor committed
to this repository yet, because the production root key has not been minted.

To activate the trust chain:

  1. On an AIR-GAPPED machine:
         bash build_system/keyceremony_root.sh /media/usb/zxv-root
     Keep root_priv.pem on that machine / encrypted removable media forever.

  2. Copy the PUBLIC outputs into this repo and commit them:
         cp /media/usb/zxv-root/ROOT_TRUST_ANCHOR.txt PROVENANCE/
         cp /media/usb/zxv-root/root_pub.pem          PROVENANCE/

  3. Publish the key-id widely (site, README, release notes, print it). Users
     verifying a download compare against the PUBLISHED key-id, not against
     anything that came with the download.

Until step 2 is done:
  - build_system/verify_release.sh warns that it cannot prove the signing key is
    yours (it still checks the signature, but nothing pins WHICH key).
  - install/install_zxv.py warns for the same reason.
Both fail closed on an actually-invalid signature; what is missing without a
pinned anchor is protection against a signature made by a DIFFERENT root key.

